==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|roa-ptg|pt}} {{term|acordar|lang=roa-ptg}}, from {{etyl|la|pt}} {{recons|accordāre|lang=la}}, present active infinitive of {{recons|accordō|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/ɐ.kuɾ.ˈðaɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|a|cor|dar}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|acord|ar}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=pt}} to [[awake]] (to gain consciousness)
# {{context|transitive|lang=pt}} to [[wake up]] (a person, an animal, etc.)
#*{{RQ:Harry Potter|3|pt-BR|page=336}}
#*:Francamente, vão '''acordar''' todo mundo!
#*::Frankly, you are going to wake up everybody!

====Conjugation====
{{pt-conj|acord|ar}}

----

==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|VL.|es}} ''*accordare'', from ''[[ac-]]'', combining form of ''[[ad]]'', 'to', +  ''[[cor]]'', 'heart', + verb suffix ''[[-are]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/akoɾˈdaɾ/|lang=es}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|acord|ar|pres=acuerdo}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=es}} to [[decide]], to [[arrange]]
# {{context|intransitive|lang=es}} to [[agree]]
#: ''Lo '''acordaron''' por unanimidad'' - "They agreed to it unanimously"
# {{context|reflexive|lang=es}} to reach agreement
'''[[acordarse]] de'''
# {{context|reflexive|lang=es}} to [[remember]], [[recall]]
#: ''¿'''Se acuerda''' Ud. '''de''' esto?'' - "Do you remember this?"

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|remember}} [[recordar]]

====Conjugation====
{{es-conj-ar (o-ue)|ac|rd}}

====Related terms====
* [[acordarse]]
* [[acorde]]
* [[acuerdo]]

